    "commit_message": "Record the 0x08002A764 lift: the unpinned-base lever and two walls\n\nThe 196-byte state copier reaches the ROM's exact length in C with 127 of\n196 bytes matching. The big lever is that a PINNED base is copied before\nevery load that uses it, while an UNPINNED local is read through\ndirectly -- which is also what puts the four long-lived record pointers in\nthe ROM's r4-r7 with no pins at all.\n\nThe note keeps the transcription and what is left: the commutative add's\noperand order (the compiler canonicalises it, not the source) and the\nclamp's two stores, which agbcc if-converts into one.",
